{"t": 1794114366.6845446, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f Regression found in production: this change replaced `round()` with `int()` in `worker/rates.py`, so conversions truncate instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. Sentry issue: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A/ (ReconciliationMismatch: expected 1100, got 1099; 2,201 events, first seen in release 2026.11.3, suspect commit 8c2f1d0). Reverting the truncation to `round(amount_minor * rate)` fixes reconciliation.", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
